/*
 * SPDX-FileCopyrightText: nirapod-sha2 contributors
 * SPDX-FileCopyrightText: nirapod-sha2 contributors
 * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 *
 * sha256_x8_compress.jinc (x86-64, avx2)
 * ======================================
 *
 * Eight independent SHA-256 compressions in AVX2, with the entry points
 * and contracts of the scalar 8-way kernel (src/sha256_x8_compress.jinc):
 *
 *     _sha256_x8_compress(h8, blocks, ms)
 *     _sha256_x8_compress_lanes(h8, in, off, n, ms)
 *
 * Lane layout: one 256-bit register holds the same word of all eight
 * instances, dword k for instance k. h8 is already in that layout (H_j of
 * instance k at 8j + k), so state register j is h8[:u256 j]. The blocks are
 * not: instance k's block is 64 contiguous bytes. Each half block (eight
 * words) of the eight instances is an 8 x 8 matrix of dwords with instances
 * as rows, and a transpose turns it into eight schedule registers:
 *
 *     VPUNPCK{L,H}_8u32   pairs of rows, interleaved dwords
 *     VPUNPCK{L,H}_4u64   quadruples of rows, interleaved qwords
 *     VPERM2I128          the two 128-bit halves: instances 0-3 and 4-7
 *
 * VPSHUFB then makes each dword big-endian (FIPS 180-4 section 3.1). Both
 * entry points transpose into a 16-word schedule window on the stack,
 * _compress from the block array and _compress_lanes straight from lane
 * memory, and run _sha256_x8_block on it.
 *
 * Rounds (_sha256_x8_block): rounds 0 to 15 are unrolled, rounds 16 to 63
 * are a loop of three passes over 16 unrolled rounds, a third of the code of
 * a full unroll, which made one-block calls slower (src/README.md, "Kernel
 * notes"); after 16 rounds the state rotation and the window are back in
 * place. AVX2 has no 32-bit rotate, so ROTR by r is a right shift, a left
 * shift by 32 - r and an XOR. Further savings per round:
 *
 *     K_t is read from a table holding it eight times, as the memory
 *     operand of the addition, instead of being broadcast
 *     Maj(a, b, c) = ((a ^ b) & (b ^ c)) ^ b, where b ^ c is the a ^ b of
 *     the round before, so Maj costs three operations
 *     T1 is accumulated in the register of h, whose old value is dead,
 *     with W_t + K_t, Ch and h added before Sigma1(e), so that e' = d + T1
 *     waits only for Sigma1
 *
 * Required CPU feature: AVX2.
 *
 * Security: h8 and the blocks are secret. Every address is fixed at
 * compile time or derived from the public round counter and the public
 * lane pointers. Residue: the local schedule window holds 16 schedule
 * words of every instance on return, W_48 .. W_63; clearing is the
 * export's obligation.
 */

/*
